Expected elements: present

All must-shows are on the image: the identity bar (chain exit "← demo" at x=24, hash, Partial badge, both stepping directions x=370–656, scrubber x=673–932, readout "128 / 1,315", phase rail x=1238–1471), a Code pane with the current position banded at y=352–374, one tab strip pairing CALL TRACE (open) with EVENT LOG, seven frames, a separate Values pane below it with ten rows, and the DATA provenance row at y=197–219 inside the transaction pane. Nothing forbidden is present.

Geometry is disciplined where it counts: every pane gap and page margin is exactly 4px, every pane title sits at 8px padding (x=13 / 930 / 1542), the call-trace opcode column right-aligns at x=1519 and the Values columns at x=1407 and x=1518.

Three things break it. The identity bar is full-bleed with 24px side padding while panes run 4+8=12px, so nothing in it aligns with anything below. Its layout gaps run 8/16/24/25/327px, with 16px doing double duty between sibling buttons and between whole objects. And the width budget is backwards: the nav column is 47% empty pane while the Code pane fades away three lines and the 383px transaction pane wraps both hashes mid-string.

I withdraw the previous round's "hard clip, no fade" on the Code pane. Measured on line 40, ink holds full strength to x=861 then ramps 216→6 over 51px. The fade is real and works. The finding is that ~6 character-cells of gradient is the only signal for ~30 hidden characters.

Rating: 6/10

